Start
/ Build one .goal file: decide which modules and actions each step uses, then let the LLM order
/ them and fill their properties, then validate and recurse into sub-goals.

- call /system/builder/EmitBuildEvent kind="goalHeader", goal=%goal%
- set %buildStart% = %Now.Ticks%
- set %trace% = {"id": "%!trace.id%", "timestamp": "%Now%", "goal": %goal%, "menu": null, "subGoals": [], "durationMs": 0}
- call Compile, on error call HandleBuildFailure
- set %trace.menu% = %menu%

- set %parentGoal% = %goal%
- foreach %parentGoal.Child%, call BuildSubGoal subGoal=%item%
- set %goal% = %parentGoal%

- math.subtract A=%Now.Ticks%, B=%buildStart%, write to %elapsedTicks%
- math.divide A=%elapsedTicks%, B=10000, write to %elapsedMs%
- set %trace.durationMs% = %elapsedMs%

- save %trace% to file '/.build/traces/%!trace.id%/%goal.Name%.json'
- add %goal.Name% to %traceGoals%
/ Re-parent indented sub-steps into the preceding condition's gate-action Child (recurses sub-goals). Post-compile, pre-save.
- build.fold Goal=%goal%, on error call HandleBuildFailure
- build.goalsSave Goal=%goal%


Compile
/ The three stages for the goal in %goal% — shared by the top goal and every sub-goal.
/ The decider answers WHICH modules and actions a step may use; that is a menu, not a sequence.
/ The LLM then decides the order, how often each is used, and what goes in their properties.
- call Decide
- foreach %goal.Step%, call Menu step=%item%
- call Properties
/ The answer must line up with the goal before any step takes its actions: one entry per step, in
/ order, each labelled with its own index — so the .pr reads like the .goal, line for line.
- build.match Goal=%goal%, Answer=%properties%, on error call FixProperties, then retry 2 times
- foreach %goal.Step%, call Settle step=%item%


Menu
/ Every module that said yes for this step, with the action chosen for it.
- set %choices% = []
- foreach %modules%, call MenuModule module=%item%
- set %menu[step.Index]% = %choices%

MenuModule
- set %key% = "s%step.Index%_%module.Name%"
- if %moduleAnswer[key].noul% is less than %threshold%, return
- if %module.Action.Count% is 1, add "%module.Name%.%module.Action[0].Name%" to %choices%
- if %module.Action.Count% is more than 1, add "%module.Name%.%actionAnswer[key].choice%" to %choices%


Settle
/ Graft and judge are one unit: a bad literal fails at the graft, a missing property at the
/ judge — either way the properties conversation gets the complaint and both run again. An else
/ written apart from its if is the programmer's to fix, not the LLM's: it never goes to the retry.
- call Apply step=%step%, on error key "ElseWithoutIf" call SourceError, on error call FixProperties, then retry 2 times


Apply
/ The step constructs its own actions from the rows the LLM answered — each born holding the step.
- set %goal.step[step.Index].code% = %properties.step[step.Index].action%
- build.validate step=%goal.step[step.Index]%


FixProperties
/ The answer was refused — it did not match the goal's steps, or a step's graft or judge rejected
/ its actions. Continue the properties conversation with the complaint (it names the step) — it is
/ the correction prompt; the retry runs the refused step again.
- call /system/builder/EmitBuildEvent kind="properties-rejected", errorMessage=%!error.Message%
- set %fixMessages% = [{"Role":"user", "Content":"Your answer was rejected by the validator: %!error.Message%\n\nReturn the corrected answer in the same shape."}]
- llm.query Message=%fixMessages%, Model="gpt-5.4-nano", cache=%!build.cache%, continuePreviousConversation=true, write to %properties%


BuildSubGoal
/ Sub-goal recursion — the same three stages, attached to the parent trace.
- set %goal% = %subGoal%
- call /system/builder/EmitBuildEvent kind="subGoalHeader", goal=%goal%
- set %subgoalStart% = %Now.Ticks%
- call Compile, on error call HandleBuildFailure
- add {goal: %goal%, menu: %menu%} to %trace.subGoals%
- math.subtract A=%Now.Ticks%, B=%subgoalStart%, write to %elapsedTicks%
- math.divide A=%elapsedTicks%, B=10000, write to %subgoalMs%
- call /system/builder/EmitBuildEvent kind="subGoalDone", goal=%goal%, subgoalMs=%subgoalMs%


SourceError
/ The programmer's plang is wrong, not the LLM's answer, so nothing is retried. The LLM writes the
/ corrected plang for the programmer; the same error is raised again carrying it, and the build of
/ this goal stops there.
- render template "/system/builder/llm/SourceFix.llm", write to %sourceFixSystem%
- set %sourceFixMessages% = [{"Role":"system", "Content":"%sourceFixSystem%"}, {"Role":"user", "Content":"%!error.Key%: %!error.Message%\n\nThe goal:\n%goal%"}]
- llm.query Message=%sourceFixMessages%, Model="gpt-5.4-nano", cache=%!build.cache%, write to %sourceFix%
- throw %!error%, fix suggestion %sourceFix%


HandleBuildFailure
/ Capture error onto trace, save, rethrow. No null-pass inference.
- call /system/builder/EmitBuildEvent kind="goalError", goal=%goal%, errorMessage=%!error.Message%, fix=%!error.FixSuggestion%
- set %trace.buildError% = {"key": "%!error.Key%", "message": "%!error.Message%", "goal": "%goal.Name%"}
- save %trace% to file '/.build/traces/%!trace.id%/%goal.Name%.json'
- throw %!error%
